  "evidence": "Original N/E/U show a sustained ~5 mm N, ~0.1 mm E, ~11 mm U offset from ~508 to ~550 (P1), followed by a sharp drop at ~550 and return toward pre-offset levels by ~551–552. P2 (545–546) is a 1-day spike inconsistent with a platform; P3 (550–550) is a single-point reversal that aligns with the return edge of P1, not an independent event. The residual plots confirm that subtracting only P1’s onset offset (Hypothesis P1) leaves no persistent bias in N/E/U after 550, while P2/P3 subtraction introduces artifacts. No evidence supports separate temporary platforms; the motion is best explained by one temporary offset (P1) with a clean return across all axes.",
  "pair_ids": ["P1"]
}
